  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nWinds will continue to be the main weather concern throughout \nSaturday morning with gusts between 30-35 in southern and central \nArizona, but should remain below advisory level winds. However, \nanother round of advisory level winds are expect in Yuma County and \nsouthern La Paz County Saturday morning, but currently allowing the \nearlier advisory to expire before reissuing to avoid confusion. \n\nAside from the wind concern, guidance is suggesting some lower end \nshower potential over the weekend. The placement of the cut-off low \nto our southwest starting Friday is expected to advect a decent mid \nand upper level moisture into the area. Some high-based light \nshowers may become possible across southern Arizona as early as \nFriday evening with best chances Saturday afternoon as the cut-off \nlow weakens and migrates over the region. Unfortunately, little if \nany measurable rainfall is expected, as most locations will struggle \nto get anything more than a trace to a few hundredths of an inch. \nThe good news though will be around a 5F-6F decrease in afternoon \nhighs on Saturday, so expect highs in the low 80s across the lower \ndeserts.\n \nBy early next week, weak upper level riding will effect the region, \nresuming near normal temperatures. Looking out even further, \nensemble guidance is hinting at another deep Pacific trough moving \ninto the Western U.S. early next week and potentially reaching our \nregion during the middle part of next week. This next weather system \ncould bring more rain chances and another cool down during the \nlatter half of next week.",
